**flags.cpp parses Windows command-line switches for case-insensitive queries.**

## Exports

`parse_flags(std::vector<std::string>&) -> void` clears/populates flags, stripping leading `-`; `has_flag(const std::string&) -> bool` lazily caches `enabled_flags` via `parsed`.

## Coupling

`CommandLineToArgvW`, `GetCommandLineW`, `LocalFree`, `string::to_lower`.